      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Primary small cell cutaneous neuroendocrine carcinoma (Merkel cell carcinoma) is an uncommon, highly malignant, primary cutaneous neuroendocrine carcinoma. Clinically it is seen as a 0.5- to 5.0-cm pinkish purple papule or nodule, usually not ulcerated, on the head, neck, or, less frequently, the roots of the limbs. We present the case of a woman with an atypical clinical presentation of a Merkel cell tumor."},
